#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ollama-land -- LAND-READY packets, the final-review lever, and the AUTO switch.

The dispatch pipeline runs from enqueue to a LAND-READY change with zero human steps. This tool
is the LAST step, behind ONE setting:

    ~/.ollama-dispatch/land-mode        REVIEW (default; file absent == REVIEW) | AUTO

REVIEW  nothing of this tool's merges/pushes to a product repo on its own. A finished chain is
        packetised (landing/<chain>/packet.{md,json}) and parked `awaiting_final_review`; the
        final reviewer (the main Claude session) reads it and runs ONE command:
            ollama-land approve <chain>            merge per repo conventions + post-land check
            ollama-land reject  <chain> --reason   close it, record why
AUTO    the same code runs the same approve step itself when every mechanical gate passes AND
        risk < threshold AND tier <= auto_max_tier AND no kill switch AND breaker closed AND the
        shadow period has enough agreements. The default is NEVER flipped by software.

Other commands: list | show | revert | go | scan | ingest | summary | stats | mode | breaker | tick
Research basis: ~/.ollama-dispatch/merge-queue/2026-10-09-autoland-research.md
"""
